# Pinggy SSH host keys, pinned for agentd's port-forwarding tunnels (P11, ADR 0022).
#
# Obtained: 2026-08-01 by scripts/tunnel/verify-provider.sh against the live service.
# Method:   ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o HashKnownHosts=no, then verified
#           with ssh-keygen -lf. Both hostnames presented the SAME 4096-bit RSA key.
# Fingerprint: SHA256:nFd5rfJMGuZXvfeRzJ/BtT3TfksAxTWMajcrHRcI7AM (RSA 4096)
#
# The service offers RSA only (its KEX offer is rsa-sha2-512,rsa-sha2-256); there is no
# ed25519 or ecdsa host key to pin. agentd passes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes with this
# file and GlobalKnownHostsFile=/dev/null, so this is the ONLY key it will trust.
#
# Rotation: when Pinggy rotates this key every tunnel fails with
#   'Host key verification failed.' -> TUNNEL_PROVIDER_UNTRUSTED. That is the intended
#   behaviour, not a bug. Follow docs/runbooks/tunnel-pinggy.md to verify and replace the
#   key out of band. Never work around it with StrictHostKeyChecking=no.
[free.pinggy.io]:443 ssh-rsa 
[pro.pinggy.io]:443 ssh-rsa 
[a.pinggy.io]:443 ssh-rsa 
